qcommon/vm_sparc: don't free the hunk-allocated instructionPointers

On 64-bit SPARC (__arch64__) VM_Compile() freed vm->instructionPointers with
Z_Free() and reallocated it with Z_Malloc(count * sizeof(void *)). That was
needed while instructionPointers was an int array from the zone. Today
VM_Create() allocates it with Hunk_Alloc() as an intptr_t array, whose
entries already have pointer size on LP64, so the block only frees a hunk
pointer: "Z_Free: freed a pointer without ZONEID", a fatal error as soon as
a QVM is compiled (vm_ui 2 etc.) on sparcv9. Remove the block.

Same fix as ioquake3 (ioq3 has the same code); for SP and MP.
32-bit SPARC and other architectures are not affected (the block is
__arch64__ only).

Upstream: not submitted yet (patch prepared for github.com/ioquake/ioq3).

--- iortcw-438e7d413b5f7277187c35b032eb0ef9093ae778/SP/code/qcommon/vm_sparc.c.orig
+++ iortcw-438e7d413b5f7277187c35b032eb0ef9093ae778/SP/code/qcommon/vm_sparc.c
@@ -1557,12 +1557,6 @@
 	fi.first = Z_Malloc(sizeof(struct src_insn));
 	fi.first->next = NULL;
 
-#ifdef __arch64__
-	Z_Free(vm->instructionPointers);
-	vm->instructionPointers = Z_Malloc(header->instructionCount *
-					   sizeof(void *));
-#endif
-
 	fi.dst_by_i_count = (struct dst_insn **) vm->instructionPointers;
 	memset(fi.dst_by_i_count, 0, header->instructionCount * sizeof(void *));
 
--- iortcw-438e7d413b5f7277187c35b032eb0ef9093ae778/MP/code/qcommon/vm_sparc.c.orig
+++ iortcw-438e7d413b5f7277187c35b032eb0ef9093ae778/MP/code/qcommon/vm_sparc.c
@@ -1557,12 +1557,6 @@
 	fi.first = Z_Malloc(sizeof(struct src_insn));
 	fi.first->next = NULL;
 
-#ifdef __arch64__
-	Z_Free(vm->instructionPointers);
-	vm->instructionPointers = Z_Malloc(header->instructionCount *
-					   sizeof(void *));
-#endif
-
 	fi.dst_by_i_count = (struct dst_insn **) vm->instructionPointers;
 	memset(fi.dst_by_i_count, 0, header->instructionCount * sizeof(void *));
 
